1.0.3 2026-10-16
  - Removed 48 individually classified root temporary Git-annex pointers: 46 resolve to zero-byte objects and two to incomplete duplicate metadata fragments without source/provenance identifiers. No recordings or sidecars changed. The remote S3 objects were not modified.
  - The current public NEMAR baseline is v1.0.1. This patch uses v1.0.3 to avoid reusing the inherited historical 1.0.2 heading below; the existing historical entry and published tags are preserved.

1.0.1 2026-10-16
  - Added the required units column to 105 raw EEG channel tables and marked 6,720 EEG rows n/a because the paper and source sidecars do not specify the stored raw .set scale. The paper’s ±100 µV epoch-rejection threshold is a preprocessing detail, not a raw-file unit declaration. BIDS 1.8.0 requires this column and encodes missing TSV values as n/a. Sources: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-026-08165-4, https://bids-specification.readthedocs.io/en/v1.8.0/02-common-principles.html, and https://bids-specification.readthedocs.io/en/v1.8.0/04-modality-specific-files/03-electroencephalography.html.
  - Added datacite.yml to .bidsignore because it is supplemental root metadata outside the BIDS filename specification; the file remains tracked. Source: https://github.com/bids-standard/bids-validator/blob/2.4.1/src/issues/list.ts.
  - Moved the existing EEG recordings and sidecars into BIDS subject/eeg directories; documented EEGReference: CPz from the acquisition paper and used BIDS 1.8.0 n/a values for unavailable raw PowerLineFrequency and SoftwareFilters metadata across 105 raw EEG sidecars. Sources: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-026-08165-4 and https://bids-specification.readthedocs.io/en/v1.8.0/04-modality-specific-files/03-electroencephalography.html. Recording payloads were unchanged.
1.1.0 2026-06-22
  - Added PLV functional connectivity matrices in CSV (comma-separated values) format alongside the existing MATLAB .mat files to improve accessibility for non-MATLAB users (Python, R, Excel).  CSV files are stored in the derivatives/plv_analysis/ directory, organized in long-format with columns: Subject, Task, Condition, ChannelA, ChannelB, TimeWindow, FreqBand, PLV.  All CSV files are identical in content to the corresponding .mat files; no new derived data have been added.
